{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "total-results": 407045, "items": [{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 13]], "date-time": "2026-09-13T17:43:23Z", "timestamp": 1789321403340, "version": "build-2803163510"}, "reference-count": 16, "publisher": "World Scientific Pub Co Pte Ltd", "issue": "02", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["Int. J. Quantum Inform."], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2004, 6]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Zurek claims to have derived Born's rule noncircularly in the context of an ontological no-collapse interpretation of quantum states, without any \"deus ex machina imposition of the symptoms of classicality\". After a brief review of Zurek's derivation it is argued that this claim is exaggerated if not wholly unjustified. In order to demonstrate that Born's rule arises noncircularly from deterministically evolving quantum states, it is not sufficient to assume that quantum states are somehow associated with probabilities and then prove that these probabilities are given by Born's rule. One has to show how irreducible probabilities can arise in the context of an ontological no-collapse interpretation of quantum states. It is argued that the reason why all attempts to do this have so far failed is that quantum states are fundamentally algorithms for computing correlations between possible measurement outcomes, rather than evolving ontological states.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1142/s0219749904000195", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2004, 6, 4]], "date-time": "2004-06-04T06:35:27Z", "timestamp": 1086330927000}, "page": "221-229", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 15, "title": ["PROBABILITIES FROM ENVARIANCE?"], "prefix": "10.1142", "volume": "02", "author": [{"given": "ULRICH", "family": "MOHRHOFF", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Sri Aurobindo International Centre of Education, Pondicherry 605002, India"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "219", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2011, 11, 21]]}, "reference": [{"key": "rf1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/RevModPhys.75.715"}, {"key": "rf2", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref", "first-page": "1793", "DOI": "10.1098/rsta.1998.0250", "volume": "356", "author": "Zurek W. H.", "journal-title": "Philos. Trans. Roy. Soc. London A"}, {"key": "rf3", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.90.120404"}, {"key": "rf4", "volume-title": "Science and Ultimate Reality: From Quantum to Cosmos", "author": "Zurek W. H.", "year": "2004"}, {"key": "rf5", "first-page": "885", "volume": "6", "author": "Gleason A. M.", "journal-title": "J. Math. Mech."}, {"key": "rf6", "unstructured": "C. A. Fuchs, Decoherence and its Implications in Quantum Computation and Information Transfer, eds. A. Gonis and P. E. A. Turchi (IOS Press, Amsterdam, 2001) pp. 38–82."}, {"key": "rf7", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.91.120403"}, {"key": "rf10", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRev.85.166"}, {"key": "rf11", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevD.34.470"}, {"key": "rf12", "volume-title": "Progress in Quantum Physics Research", "author": "Mohrhoff U.", "year": "2004"}, {"key": "rf13", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1023/A:1019727521587"}, {"key": "rf14", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1142/S0217732302007533"}, {"key": "rf15", "volume-title": "Foundations of Quantum Mechanics", "author": "Jauch J. M.", "year": "1968"}, {"key": "rf16", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1023/B:FOOP.0000012010.89014.f4"}, {"key": "rf17", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1023/A:1019775404748"}, {"key": "rf18", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1142/S0219749904000183"}], "container-title": ["International Journal of Quantum Information"], "language": "en", "link": [{"URL": 